# {{project_name}} — Sprint Tracker

This directory is your project's **live** sprint tracker. The framework
WarpOS ships the schemas and templates; everything in this directory is
written by `/sprint:*` commands as you actually run sprints.

Do not edit `current-sprint.yaml` or `sprint-progress.yaml` by hand
unless you know what you're doing — they are the source of truth for
crash recovery and resume.

## What lives where

| Path | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `current-sprint.yaml` | Live current sprint state |
| `sprint-progress.yaml` | Crash recovery checkpoint — read on resume |
| `plan-contracts/<id>.yaml` | One Plan Contract per `/sprint:plan` |
| `requirements/<sprint>/...` | PRD, stories, COPY, INPUTS, TRACE, AC, QA, redteam, release plans |
| `tickets/<id>.yaml` | One file per ticket |
| `issues/<id>.yaml` | Structured per-issue YAML; human-readable companion is repo-root `issues.md` |
| `external-services/<id>.yaml` | Third-party service readiness records |
| `approvals/<id>.yaml` | Approval decisions |
| `decisions/<id>.yaml` | Sprint-scope decisions |
| `releases/<id>.yaml` | Release artifacts |
| `ralph/<sprint>/progress.yaml` | Active Ralph loop state |
| `checkpoints/<sprint>-<n>.yaml` | Frozen checkpoints |
| `history/<sprint>/` | Closed sprint archive |

## Getting started

```
/sprint:plan "<brief plain-language request>"
```

Then follow the next-recommended-command in the produced Plan Contract.

## Resume after a crash

```
/sprint:plan        # for a fresh start
# or read sprint-progress.yaml#resume_command and run that instead
```

See `_docs/sprint/CRASH_RECOVERY.md` in the WarpOS framework for the
full resume procedure.

## Adoption note

This tracker is downstream live state. It is intentionally NOT shipped
inside the WarpOS framework repo itself — only the templates and
schemas are. See `_docs/sprint/FRAMEWORK_VS_DOWNSTREAM.md` for the
boundary.
